---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL } from '../config';
---

<Page
  title="About AnyAirDrop.com: Free File Sharing Between Any Devices"
  description="AnyAirDrop.com sends files between phones and computers over your Wi-Fi, in the browser. Learn how it works, what our server sees, and who is behind it."
  heading="About AnyAirDrop.com"
  lead="AnyAirDrop.com sends files between iPhones, Android phones, Windows PCs, Macs and Linux computers over your Wi-Fi, right in the browser. No app, no account, no upload."
  type="AboutPage"
>
  <h2>Why it exists</h2>
  <p>
    Sending a photo or a video from one device to another is harder than it should be when the two devices come from
    different companies. AnyAirDrop.com is a small, free tool that makes it one tap: open the page on both devices, tap the
    other one, and the files go straight across.
  </p>

  <h2>How your files travel</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Device to device.</strong> When both devices can reach each other, your browser connects directly to the other
      browser and sends the file. It never passes through our server and is never stored anywhere.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Encrypted.</strong> The browser encrypts every connection it opens. Nothing starts until the receiving device
      taps Accept.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No size limit from us.</strong> Large files stream in pieces, so a long video does not have to fit in memory.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>If a network blocks direct connections,</strong> an encrypted relay can carry the transfer instead, and the
      page tells you when that is happening.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What our server sees</h2>
  <p>
    Our server only introduces devices to each other. To do that it briefly sees a random device name (like “Sage Finch”), the
    kind of device and browser, and either a hashed match of the shared network or the pairing code you typed. It never sees
    your files or their names.
  </p>
  <p>
    Like any website, the companies that host it keep standard technical logs, such as IP addresses. We do not run ads or
    trackers on the transfer screen, and there is nothing to sign up for.
  </p>

  <h2>Independent and open source</h2>
  <p>
    AnyAirDrop.com is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Apple Inc. or any other
    device maker. The code is open source under the MIT license, so you can read exactly what it does:
    <a href={GITHUB_URL}>AnyAirDrop on GitHub</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>Found a bug, or have an idea? Visit the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</Page>
